 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you? Shoot them with lot of light and face the light at an angle so it doesn't look harsh. Use a microphone if available. Then you' need online backup, like Zoom or skype. Shoot in room with window so the internet connects as fast as it can, and use wireless headphones so you can hear each other. Try using headphones with the audio coming from your computer rather than the video feed. It' a lot smoother. Shoot straight at each other so your faces fill most of the frame. It feels a lot more engaged than shoulder to shoulder.",
